{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"The main simplification is to avoid the `WithLp` embedding and its Cauchy–Schwarz/nlinarith argument. The scalar function `x ↦ ⟪f x, f x₀⟫` is already continuous and strictly positive at `x₀`, so continuity directly supplies a positive ball; one bump function on that ball finishes the measure argument."}}
